        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel pounds Beirut, deepening the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon Middle East Issued on: 15/03/2026 - 10:44 Overnight strikes in southern Lebanon killed at least four people, Lebanese state media and the government said on Sunday. Israel is fighting a second front in the war in the Middle East in southern Lebanon, against Hezbollah, alongside the air campaign against Iran it launched with the United States more than two weeks ago. Lebanon's state-run National News Agency (NNA) said Israel struck \"an apartment in a residential building\" in a northern district of the coastal city of Sidon, killing one person and causing a fire. Story by Morgan Ayre and Thibaut Franceschet. Undercover in Iran: How French spies gather Intelligence in the Middle East 15/03/2026 Middle East Donald Trump says will open Strait of Hormuz \"one way or another\" 15/03/2026 Middle East Iranian strikes, Hezbollah rockets make regular life in Israel ‘simply impossible’ 14/03/2026 Middle East UN force base in southern Lebanon comes under fire, one peacekeeper wounded 14/03/2026 Middle East US embassy attacked in Baghdad, after strikes kill Iran-backed fighters in Iraq 14/03/2026 Middle East Israel and Lebanon are expected to hold direct talks in the coming days 14/03/2026 Middle East Israel threatens to strike ambulances in Lebanon in Hezbollah fighting 14/03/2026 Middle East Why did the US military bomb the strategic Iranian island of Kharg? 14/03/2026 Middle East Why did the US bomb Kharg Island? What is its significance for Iran? 14/03/2026 Middle East"
